    A15_SMSS_71_M016935_032                                                   
                                                                              
    Apollo 15 Soil Mechanics                                                  
    Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page E-2                         
                                                                              
    Plot of Pre-Flight Penetration Calibration Tests                          
                                                                              
    This handdrawn plot shows the results of a pre-flight calibration test    
    of the actual vs. recorded penetration for Lunar Self-Recording           
    Penetrometer (LSRP) drum S/N 2005.  The actual penetration in             
    centimeters is shown on the ordinate, ranging from 0 to 80. The recorded  
    penetration on the drum in centimeters, from 0 to 2.5, is on the          
    abscissa.  The five test points form a straight line.  A notation         
    "Actual/Recorded ~ 31.40 to 31.50 appears at the top. The test was done   
    at U.C. Berkeley and the date listed is "6-24-70", but this must be an    
    error, the test was probably done on 24 June 1971, not 1970.  Note that   
    the test is for "SRP DRUM S/N 2005" the lunar drum used on Apollo 15 was  
    S/N 2002.                                                                 
                                                                              
